{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Force/reason surface audit + ruling (A) — normalization design (2026-08-18)\n\nOperator rulings this session, in order, converged on:\n- `--force[=<reason>]` is THE universal approved write pattern. The audit reason is tightly coupled to the force operation (it belongs on the audit record), so it rides INLINE on `--force`, NOT on a separate `--reason`. This REVERSED an interim decoupling proposal.\n- `force_close` is to be REMOVED (its force-close audit reason is carried by `--force=<reason>` on a close).\n- `force` is allowed through any command surface; auditability comes from the fact that a force op yields NO signed attestation (projects can gate on certification in CI).\n- Blast radius for this normalization is limited to **transition + claim** (both externally-exposed surfaces — lib/CLI/MCP — AND internal module/method naming, AND transition/claim guidance text). tracker-maintenance / init / gates break-glass `--force` for OTHER commands are OUT of scope.\n\n### Canonical model: `claim` already has the target shape\nlib `claim(force: str | None = None)` — the value IS the audit reason; bare CLI `--force` -> \"(no reason given)\", `--force=<reason>` -> that reason. Everything else normalizes to this.\n\n### Audit findings (the divergences to fix)\n1. **transition lib** splits one concept across `force: bool` + separate `reason: str` + redundant `force_close: str|None` (_lib_writes.py ~228-240). Target: `force: str | None` like claim; drop bool + force_close.\n2. **transition CLI** lets `--reason` stand in as the force-bypass note (transition.py help ~42-46, 59-63) — a coupling claim lacks. Target: force note from `--force=<reason>` only; `--reason` = close_reason only.\n3. **Internal naming drift** — the single \"force-bypass reason\" concept is spelled 4 ways: `force_reason` (CLI _parse_flags), `force_close` (lib param), `force_close_reason` (txn.py plumbing + a PERSISTED status_data key, txn.py ~197/250/318/371-372), `force_plan_review` (claim_compute). Target: unify IN-MEMORY names to `force_reason`; RETAIN the persisted `force_close_reason` status key (durable reduced state; renaming = event-schema migration, out of scope).\n4. **Guidance text** — gates.py (~302-303) prints two spellings in one override hint: `claim --force=\"<reason>\"` AND the decoupled `transition --force --reason=\"<reason>\"`. Target: unify both to `--force[=<reason>]`. (txn.py override hints ~554/602/618 already show `--force=\"<reason>\"`.)\n5. **Close-gate keying** — the completion-verify close gate keys on `force_close` specifically (close_precheck.py ~566, transition_close.py ~440), NOT on `force`. Consolidating requires rewiring these to `force is not None`.\n6. **MCP** transition_ticket/claim_ticket lack force/reason/caused_by/ref (docstrings assert a now-void no-force policy). Handled by sibling scratchy-leprous-galago (already certified); MCP `force` follows the same reason-carrying str.\n\n### Migration / back-compat\n- lib `force_close=\"<r>\"` -> WARN via the sanctioned lib-kind deprecation alias (_deprecations `_KINDS` includes `lib`) and map to `force=\"<r>\"`; `force=True` -> `force=\"(no reason given)\"`. There is no lib/cli hard-tombstone (only env/cfg/file tombstone), so a warn+map alias is the correct retirement path for the kwarg.\n- Reducer/schema UNCHANGED: historical events (incl. `force_close_reason` status field) reduce to identical state.\n\n### Ticket mapping (all discovered_from cranial-goodly-seahog)\n- blusterous-earthly-kitten (task) — the normalization above (lib + CLI + guidance + internal naming; remove force_close). Foundational.\n- churlish-fruited-dassie (story, depends_on blusterous) — mechanical argparse refactor preserving the POST-blusterous `--force[=<reason>]` surface.\n- topaz-blubbery-mice (story) — Pattern-B conformance oracle; contract asserts `force` (str, `--force[=<reason>]`) + reason + caused_by + ref + close_class; `force_close` excluded.\n- scratchy-leprous-galago (bug, CERTIFIED) — MCP parity; force is the reason-carrying str delegating to the normalized lib.\n- linen-contrived-wisent (task, depends_on scratchy) — docs."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787089870915986001,"uuid":"42a89228-f133-4343-b540-c3c34ec2c99f"}